<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–1990</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bonn Republic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> was the common English name for the Federal Republic of Germany between its foundation in 1949 and German reunification in 1990. Formed from the American, British and French occupation zones with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a> as its capital, it became a parliamentary democracy and a member of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-economic-community">European Economic Community</a>. Its rapid post-war recovery became known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wirtschaftswunder">Wirtschaftswunder</a>, or economic miracle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-germany.jpg" alt="West Germany" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:SKopp, User:Madden, and other users · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
